@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/driver#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .
@prefix execution: <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .

<> a orexis:SelfGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHO THIS AGENT IS: the dispatcher, and this document is its own by the self it states. Booted as
#  "dispatcher", the agent checks that this is so.
#
#  WHAT IT RUNS: it plans the parcels' routes through the driver it has and walks them, in the
#  packages' words, since the courier's domain has none for an agent. Its world ships no rules, so it
#  is no deliberator.

:dispatcher a orexis:Self , planning:Planner , execution:Executor .

#  WHAT ITS SEARCH MAY SPEND IN A PASS, a stance (knowledge/domain/kernel/stance.md): the two parcels
#  are one want, coupled through the one driver, whose search costs 191 candidates (measure-the-search),
#  past planning's 32 and past 128 too. `tests/test_driver.py` boots this world with no budget of its
#  own and finds the eleven-step plan in one pass at this figure, and walks it.
:dispatcher planning:budget 256 .
